shape: Tapered Directional/Directional
flex direction: Directional Flex (increases pop in tail with stiffer nose for easier control in all conditions)
camber type: Directional Camber (rocker in nose for extra float in powder, retaining response and stability of traditional camber)
width options: Standard, Wide
mounting system: The Channel (Burton Channel system for fine-tuned stance width and freedom in stance location, compatible with most major binding brands, works best with Burton EST bindings)
available lengths: 152cm, 156cm, 160cm, 156cm Wide
designer collaboration: Designed in partnership with Selema Masekela
laminate: Triax with Carbon I-Beam (triax fiberglass above and below core for versatile flex and consistent response, ultralight Carbon I-Beam backbone on bottom layer to increase pop)
core: Super Fly II 700G Core (stronger and lighter woods targeted in specific areas for more pop and strength while reducing weight)
core zones: Dualzone EGD (wood grain aligned along heel and toe edge in two unbroken zones perpendicular to rest of core for consistent edge hold and strength)
core sections: Squeezebox (thicker more powerful sections combined with thinner more flexible sections throughout core for enhanced energy transfer, snappier and more stable)
base: Sintered WFO (Wide F!#@ing Open - extra absorbent, high density sintered material infused with specially formulated wax, ultra durable)
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin reducing carbon footprint by 50% over conventional petroleum-based epoxies)
freeride geometry: Balanced Freeride Geometry (setback camber and stance-centred sidecut makes board feel like twin when riding flat based, with tight turns and effortless float of directional board)
terrain: Groomers, fresh powder, all mountain, freeride
riding style: Surf-inspired freeride, carving, powder
